{
  "requirement": "After one valid judgment, the harness MUST write the subject text, submitted\ndetermination and rationale, and recorded inputs using the existing evidence\nschema. {cite}`requirements.ci.schema`\nBy default, it MUST write the subject's evidence file. With `--stdout`, it MUST\nemit a single evidence JSON object followed by a newline to stdout and MUST NOT\ncreate or change evidence files or directories. All three outcomes MUST be\nwritten to the selected destination as completed assessments; their validation\nstatus MUST follow {cite}`requirements.ci.determination`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Determination: true.** The `{impl}`-marked code implements each obligation of `requirements.authoring.persistence`, and the `{test}`-marked tests cover the main points in the design space. I found no unmarked code that implements part of the requirement and no unspecified behavior in the marked code.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Record contents.** `assess` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`) builds the record only after exactly one valid `submit_judgment`. It contains the subject text under the `requirement` or `example` key, `determination` from `Judgment::to_value`, the `rationale`, and `inputs` from `sources.recorded_inputs()`. `to_value` (`src/judgment.rs`) maps true, false and `{\"FIXME\": [...]}` to the existing schema forms. Outline inputs store only `file`, `item` and `hash`, as `requirements.ci.schema` requires.\n- **Default destination.** `configured_assessment` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`) writes the record to `evidence/<subject>.json` in `EvidenceOutput::File` mode. It creates the directory if needed. The batch path, `write_record` (`src/authoring/batch.rs`), writes the same file through a temporary file and an atomic persist. The atomicity is not required by this requirement, but `write_record` also implements `requirements.authoring.batch`, whose concurrent assessments read these files.\n- **`--stdout`.** `EvidenceOutput::Stdout` writes one pretty-printed JSON object plus `\"\\n\"` to stdout and returns `evidence_path = None`. No evidence file or directory is created or changed on this path. The usage log is kept outside the repository, and `author_evidence_with_output` refuses a state directory inside the project.\n- **All three outcomes.** True, false and FIXME all go through the same write path, so each is stored as a completed assessment. The `persisted` method (`src/authoring/mod.rs`) marks usage as `completed` with `evidence_written` set.\n- **Validation status.** Validation follows `requirements.ci.determination` in the validator, not in the authoring code. The authoring code only needs to emit the existing schema, which it does.\n\n**Tests**\n- `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files` covers true, false and FIXME with `--stdout`. It also covers a project with no `evidence` directory and verbose mode. It checks that stdout parses as a single JSON object ending in a newline, and that the schema fields and input forms are present. It also checks that the original evidence file is byte-identical, that no `evidence` directory was created, and that usage reports `evidence_output` as `stdout`.\n- `false_is_a_completed_assessment` and `verbose_single_author_reports_only_false_rationale_without_source_inputs` cover file-mode persistence of false and true. They check the recorded rationale and determination, that outline inputs carry `item` and `hash` but no source text, and that usage is `completed`.\n- The batch tests `terminal_progress_distinguishes_judgments_from_authoring_errors`, `denied_read_aborts_only_its_assessment_and_runs_queued_assessments` and `denied_read_preserves_in_flight_assessments_and_their_evidence` cover persisted true, false and FIXME records. They also check that a failed or denied assessment writes no evidence.\n- `explicit_untracked_reads_abort_without_another_request_or_evidence_write` checks that an aborted assessment leaves the evidence file unchanged.\n- `failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage` covers a failed write: the command fails and usage records `evidence_written: false` while keeping the FIXME determination.\n- `live_bedrock_authoring` exercises a real provider with `--stdout` and checks that no `evidence` directory is created.\n\nNo source comment acknowledges a gap against this requirement.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.persistence",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.persistence"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} persistence",
        "After one valid judgment, the harness MUST write the subject text, submitted",
        "determination and rationale, and recorded inputs using the existing evidence",
        "schema. {cite}`requirements.ci.schema`",
        "By default, it MUST write the subject's evidence file. With `--stdout`, it MUST",
        "emit a single evidence JSON object followed by a newline to stdout and MUST NOT",
        "create or change evidence files or directories. All three outcomes MUST be",
        "written to the selected destination as completed assessments; their validation",
        "status MUST follow {cite}`requirements.ci.determination`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.schema",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.schema"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} schema",
        "A requirement or example evidence file at `evidence/<full-name>.json` MUST be a JSON object with exactly `requirement` or `example`, `determination`, `rationale`, and `inputs`. The definition text and rationale MUST be nonempty strings, `determination` MUST use one of the outcomes defined by {cite}`requirements.ci.outcomes`, and `inputs` MUST be an array. Every evidence input MUST have exactly one of three forms: an outline input with `file`, `item`, and `hash`; a requirements input with `requirements`, `matches`, and `text`; or a definition input with `definition` and `text`. File paths MUST resolve to permitted inputs under {cite}`requirements.ci.input_containment`. Project-local paths SHOULD be recorded relative to the project for portability; absolute and parent-relative paths MAY be used when their resolved targets are permitted. `matches` MUST be an array of distinct full definition names, `hash` MUST be a lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 digest, and `text` MUST be a nonempty array of strings. Evidence MUST NOT store source text for outline inputs.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.determination",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.determination"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} determination",
        "For requirement and example evidence, both `true` and `FIXME` MUST satisfy the determination check in `habeas::validate()`. A false determination MUST fail validation and be reported with its rationale. Each definition's determination MUST be checked on its own; a false determination MUST NOT fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. All other evidence checks MUST still pass: FIXME MUST NOT excuse malformed, missing, or stale evidence or uncovered references. Validation MUST check the recorded outcome, schema, input freshness, and reference coverage without inference or reassessing whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap.",
        ":::"
      ]
